update public.moo_versions set body_md = body_md || E'| EOC logbook                      | Chronological event/decision/action record, category, time, author and correction reference.                                   | Append-only; corrections are new linked entries, not overwrites.                  |\n| Decision log                     | Issue, options, evidence, decision-maker, decision, rationale, time, implementing owner and follow-up.                         | Decision authority stated; avoid ambiguous “approved” entries.                    |\n| Barangay situation report        | Barangay identifier, report time, condition, aggregate counts, needs, source and verification.                                 | Blank count means “not reported”, not zero. Avoid personal names.                 |\n| SitRep                           | Reporting period, hazard/incident, situation, impact, actions, resources, needs, constraints, map/data status and next steps.  | Use current approved DILG VIII/NDRRMC format and reporting cut-offs.              |\n| Resource request and status      | Requesting entity, item/service, quantity, purpose, priority, location, decision, source, mobilisation, delivery and closeout. | Follow Chapter 5 and the approved request workflow; status progression traceable. |\n| Operational briefing / handover  | Situation, objectives, risks, tasks, requests, decisions, contacts, reporting and open issues.                                 | Outgoing and incoming officers acknowledge handover.                              |\n| After-action / corrective action | Finding, evidence, cause, action, owner, due date, resource and verification.                                                  | Do not close action without evidence and authorised verification.                 |\n\n## 11.2 Reporting and Situation Reports\n\nThe EOC shall prepare and submit pre-disaster, during-disaster, post-disaster and terminal reports using the current approved reporting template and instructions of DILG Region VIII, OCD and NDRRMC as applicable. Chapter 1 cites regional reporting cut-offs in its proposed EOC staffing table; these times shall not be treated as confirmed until the responsible regional office validates the current template and reporting instruction.\n\nThe SitRep shall identify the reporting period and data cut-off; distinguish new developments from cumulative totals; cite sources and verification status; describe affected areas and population; summarise actions and resources; identify gaps and urgent decisions; and state the next reporting time. An absent or blank report shall not be converted to zero. Estimates shall be labelled and accompanied by method or source where available.\n\nFrom the raising of Blue, the City EOC uses the harmonized reporting template. Reports are pre-disaster, during, post-disaster and terminal, each with a narrative and a detailed breakdown. The LGU submits to the Province on or before 06:00 and 18:00 at White, and 09:00 and 19:00 at Blue and Red (Figure 4.4). SOP 4-08 sets the cut-off from these times.\n\n**Figure 4.4**\n\n*Reporting Deadlines by Alert Status*\n\n![Figure 4: 11.2 Reporting and Situation Reports](/library/ch4v11/fig-04.webp)\n\n*Note.* From Table 3, Frequency of Reporting, of the DILG VIII Disaster Response Reporting Template and SOP (RDRRMC VIII Resolution No. 12-006, s. 2023; DILG VIII Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008). The City deadline is the LGU-to-Province row; the others show where the report goes next.\n\n## 11.3 Privacy, Information Security and Record Integrity\n\n- Collect only the information necessary for the operational purpose and approved reporting requirement. Avoid names of evacuees, patients, informants and vulnerable persons in general-purpose EOC records.\n\n- Keep detailed beneficiary, patient, protection and household-level records with the authorised custodian under documented access and sharing rules. Use aggregated or de-identified information in general situation products and public maps.\n\n- Apply role-based access, secure transmission, approved storage, device and account controls, retention rules and incident reporting in accordance with RA 10173 and City policy.\n\n- Preserve source, timestamp, responsible person, validation status and amendment history for records supporting statutory decisions or public reporting.\n\n- In MODE, local capture and queued records are not equivalent to a server-confirmed authority action. EOC level changes and other authorised decisions require an online connection and must not be represented as approved while offline.\n\n- Logbook entries are append-only; corrections must reference the original entry. Approved records and closed workflows follow the repository''s integrity guards and retention arrangements.\n\n# 12. Resource Coordination and External Assistance Interface\n\nThis chapter covers operational identification, coordination and status tracking of response resources. Budget execution, procurement, accounting, property and fund disbursement controls are governed by Chapter 5 and the applicable laws and City procedures. The EOC may identify and prioritise operational needs within its coordination role, but it shall not replace the financial and procurement authorities.\n\n53. Receive a request through the approved EOC or incident command channel and record requesting office/agency, location, purpose, item/service, quantity, urgency, required time and supporting information.\n\n54. Check whether the request is complete, within the requesting entity''s mandate, and linked to an incident objective or approved protective action. Seek clarification where necessary.\n\n55. Coordinate with the resource/Logistics function and relevant asset owners to determine availability, condition, location, constraints and estimated mobilisation.\n\n56. Refer approval, procurement, transfer or expenditure decisions to the authorised official/office under Chapter 5. Record the decision and its authority.\n\n57. Track approved requests through mobilisation, dispatch, receipt/delivery, use, return/demobilisation and closeout. Record partial fulfilment and unmet balance.\n\n58. Escalate requests that cannot be fulfilled locally through the approved mutual aid, provincial/regional or national assistance route. Record the receiving authority and response.\n\n59. Reconcile resource status and custody records after operations. Feed shortages, damage, expiry, replenishment and supplier issues into readiness and investment planning.\n\n| VALIDATION NOTE. Do not use this chapter to create procurement thresholds, emergency purchasing powers, mutual-aid commitments or expenditure authority. These are governed by Chapter 5, RA 12009 and applicable implementing rules, COA and City financial controls. |\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n\n# 13. Transition, Demobilisation and Early Recovery Handover\n\nResponse stabilisation does not automatically mean that all needs have been resolved. The EOC Manager shall coordinate with the Incident Commander/IMT, CDRRMO Head, Mayor/CDRRMC and sector offices to identify activities that must continue, the institution that assumes responsibility, resource and information transfer, and any statutory reporting or funding obligations. Recovery and rehabilitation actions are developed under Chapter 8; monitoring, learning and institutional improvement are addressed under Chapter 7.\n\n**Table 4.15**\n\n*Transition and Handover Domains*\n\n| **Handover domain**                  | **Required transfer / record**                                                                                       | **Receiving owner**                                                                     |\n|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Outstanding life-safety actions      | Unresolved threats, missing persons status where verified, unsafe areas, ongoing rescue/medical/protection activity. | Incident Commander / lead response agency                                               |\n| Displacement and services            | Aggregate displacement status, shelter/CCCM needs, health/WASH/protection, return and durable-solution issues.       | CSWDO / CHO / relevant sector office                                                    |\n| Infrastructure and lifelines         | Damage/status, isolation, priority restoration, dependencies and technical assessment requirements.                  | Asset owners, City Engineering, utilities and competent agencies                        |\n| Resources and finance                | Custody, delivery, outstanding requests, committed resources, costs/obligations and records.                         | Resource owners; Budget/Accounting/Property/Purchasing under Chapter 5                  |\n| Information and public communication | Validated situation data, source files, maps, outstanding corrections and authorised public messages.                | CDRRMO/EOC records custodian and designated public information office                   |\n| Recovery and continuity              | Essential service interruptions, alternate arrangements, repair priorities and recovery recommendations.             | Continuity executive, sector offices, CPDO and recovery coordination body as designated |\n| Reporting and review                 | Terminal report, after-action review, corrective action register and record index.                                   | CDRRMO Head / CDRRMC oversight and relevant offices                                     |\n\n# 14. Standard Operating Procedures\n\nThe following procedures provide the minimum control sequence. Before adoption, the CDRRMO shall reconcile them with the current official EOC and ICS manuals, valid City EOC/ICS issuances, approved contingency plans and the IAT v1.6 Action Plan (Annex 4-A). Each procedure shall be converted into a controlled protocol and tested through a tabletop, functional or full-scale exercise as appropriate.\n\nFigure 4.5 places the nine procedures in the operating phases. Each procedure has a control block (type, the MODE protocol that carries it, the legal decision authority kept apart from the operational owner, trigger, forms, indicators and policy basis) and a step table. Every step states its actor, action, decision or criteria, inputs, outputs and records, timing, control and escalation.\n\n**Figure 4.5**\n\n*Chapter 4 Procedures by Operating Phase*\n\n![Figure 5: 14. Standard Operating Procedures](/library/ch4v11/fig-05.webp)\n\n*Note.* Form codes are those of section 18; where MODE already had a form, it is used under its MODE code (Table 4.37).\n\n## SOP 4-01 \\| Official warning receipt, verification and escalation\n\nProcess owner: CDRRMO Operations and Warning Division / designated duty officer. Purpose: Ensure that incoming official warning products and significant local reports are authenticated, time-stamped, interpreted within their source limits and escalated to the correct decision-maker.\n\n**Table 4.16**\n\n*SOP 4-01 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                 |\n|---------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-WARNING-RECEIPT (6 steps, new in MODE 1.11)                                                  |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Not applicable: receipt and verification take no legal decision                                           |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Operations and Warning (OpCen duty officer); escalation to the CDRRMO Head                         |\n| **Trigger**                     | Receipt of an official product or a significant local report                                              |\n| **Forms**                       | EWR-F01 (MODE EOC-WARN-01)                                                                                |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | A6.1 (score 3, Medium); B4.3 (score 2, Medium)                                                            |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A6.1: MR-06; B4.3: MR-09                                                                                  |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 12(c); DILG VIII Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008 (RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006, s. 2023) |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP HR-05 (duty); SOP 4-02, 4-03                                                                          |\n\n**Table 4.17**\n\n*SOP 4-01 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Receive</td>\n<td>Duty officer (OpCen)</td>\n<td><p>Receive the product or report through the approved channel; keep the original file or link.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is the source on the source register?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Official product or local report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Warning receipt log, EWR-F01 (MODE EOC-WARN-01); source copy</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On receipt; continuous on duty</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Issue time and local receipt time both recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Duty supervisor if the channel fails</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Authenticate</td>\n<td>Duty officer</td>\n<td><p>Confirm issuing agency, product number and title, issue time, validity, coverage and update or cancellation status.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Authentic and current? If not, ask the source; never relay it as official</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Product; source register</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Verification checklist</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Immediately after receipt</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Agency wording kept unchanged</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Source agency for a doubtful product</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Classify</td>\n<td>Duty officer</td>\n<td><p>Classify as official warning or advisory, verified observation, partner report or unverified report.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Category as defined in section 6.1; uncertainty labelled</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Verification result</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Source and verification status</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before escalation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> An unverified report is never labelled official</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head when the class affects action</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Assess local relevance</td>\n<td>Duty officer with Research and Planning</td>\n<td><p>Identify places, exposed people and assets, critical dependencies and the relevant contingency plan.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which plan or scenario applies?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> CDRA layers; Chapter 3 registers; CP register</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Initial impact note</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before escalation, except life-safety</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source of each local fact stated</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Technical office for interpretation</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Escalate</td>\n<td>Duty officer</td>\n<td><p>Notify the CDRRMO Head or duty supervisor and the affected focal persons under the approved escalation matrix.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Life-safety concern? Use urgent channels at once, without waiting for a full report</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Impact note; escalation matrix</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Notification and acknowledgement log</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Immediately</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Acknowledgement recorded for each notice</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head; Mayor/CDRRMC and EOC Manager where action or activation is implicated</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Update</td>\n<td>Duty officer</td>\n<td><p>Record changed, superseding or cancelled products and notify recipients of material revisions.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Material change?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> New or superseding product</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Updated log and message trail</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On each new product</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Superseded products marked, not deleted</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> As step 5</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** Continuous while on duty; update immediately upon receipt of a new or superseding source product. Review source directory at the interval approved by the CDRRMO Head.\n\n**Escalation:** CDRRMO Head; relevant source agency for disputed technical interpretation; Mayor/CDRRMC and EOC Manager where approved actions or activation are implicated.\n\n**Minimum records:** Warning receipt log; source copy/reference; verification checklist; initial impact note; notification/acknowledgement log.\n\n## SOP 4-02 \\| Warning-to-action decision and dissemination\n\nProcess owner: CDRRMO Head / designated warning and public information focal person; decision authority remains with the competent official. Purpose: Translate verified warning information into authorised, actionable and accessible local messages and protective actions.\n\n**Table 4.18**\n\n*SOP 4-02 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-WARNING-DISSEM (7 steps); short-lead hazards: PR-FLASHFLOOD-EARLY                             |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | The official or body named in law, the EOC EO or the approved CP                                           |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head / warning and public information focal person                                                  |\n| **Trigger**                     | A validated matrix trigger or decision need                                                                |\n| **Forms**                       | EWR-F02 (Annex 4-C register); EWR-F03 (MODE EOC-WARN-02); ER-F04                                           |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | A6.2 (score 2, High); A6.3 (score 2, High); A6.4 (score 4, Low); A6.5 (score 2, Low); A6.7 (score 0, High) |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A6.2: MR-06, MR-16; A6.3: MR-06; A6.4: MR-06; A6.5: MR-06; A6.7: MR-06, MR-16                              |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 12(c); RA 11106 (Filipino Sign Language); DILG VIII Res. No. 12-006 Table 2                  |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 4-01, 4-06; SOP GOV-05 (public notice of a SOID)                                                       |\n\n**Table 4.19**\n\n*SOP 4-02 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Open action record</td>\n<td>Warning and public information focal person</td>\n<td><p>Link the verified warning to the approved hazard-specific warning-action matrix and scenario.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is there an approved matrix entry? If not, treat it as a decision need (step 2)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SOP 4-01 output; matrix register (Annex 4-C); CP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Warning-action record (EWR-F02 register entry)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On a validated trigger or decision need</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Only adopted matrix entries are used</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Identify the decision</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head with the focal person</td>\n<td><p>State options, affected area, lead time, likely impacts, uncertainty and the office for each action.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> What decision is needed, and by whom?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Impact note; PDRA (SOP 4-03)</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Decision brief</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Uncertainty stated, not hidden</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Source agency for technical clarification</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Route for approval</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head</td>\n<td><p>Submit the recommendation to the designated authority; record approval, change, refusal or request for information.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> The designated authority decides</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Decision brief</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Authorised decision record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Decision-maker, basis, time and scope recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC where required</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Prepare the message</td>\n<td>Focal person</td>\n<td><p>Draft source, time, hazard, area, effective time, required action, accessible instructions and feedback channel.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Technical meaning preserved?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Decision record; templates</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Message version</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once after the decision</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Local language and accessible formats (A6.4)</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Public information focal person</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Approve and disseminate</td>\n<td>Approving official; focal person</td>\n<td><p>Obtain the message approval; send through primary and backup channels and barangay relays.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved before release</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Approved message</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Dissemination log, EWR-F03 (MODE EOC-WARN-02)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once after approval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Channel and time recorded for each send</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head if a channel fails</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Confirm receipt</td>\n<td>Focal person with barangay liaison</td>\n<td><p>Seek acknowledgement from barangays, facilities and agencies; use alternate channels where receipt fails.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Transmission is not receipt: every failure followed up</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Dissemination log</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Acknowledgement and failed-delivery register</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Until all targets confirm</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Unconfirmed targets listed by name of barangay or facility</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Barangay or BDRRMC through an alternate channel</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Monitor and correct</td>\n<td>Focal person; public information</td>\n<td><p>Track actions, questions, rumours and changes; correct through the same authorised route.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Correction or superseding message needed?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Feedback; new products</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Feedback, correction and closure record (ER-F04)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Until closure</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Prior message versions kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Approving authority</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** Initiate as soon as a validated matrix trigger or decision need arises; refresh on material change or scheduled review in the contingency plan.\n\n**Escalation:** Designated approving authority; CDRRMO Head; City Mayor/CDRRMC where required; source agency on technical clarification; City public information focal person.\n\n**Minimum records:** Warning-action record; decision brief; authorised decision; message versions; dissemination and acknowledgement logs; correction record.\n\n## SOP 4-03 \\| Heightened preparedness and PDRA coordination\n\nProcess owner: CDRRMO Head; Research and Planning and Operations and Warning Divisions jointly coordinate. Purpose: Organise a documented assessment and readiness process when a warning or verified observation indicates an increasing risk.\n\n**Table 4.20**\n\n*SOP 4-03 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                               |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-PDRA (6 steps)                                             |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Decisions by the authorised officials; SOID only through SOP GOV-05     |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO Head; Research and Planning with Operations and Warning          |\n| **Trigger**                     | An approved warning or scenario trigger                                 |\n| **Forms**                       | EWR-F04 (MODE GOV-F09)                                                  |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | A8.6 (score 3, Medium); A8.8 (score 1, High); B1.2 (score 3, Medium)    |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A8.6: MR-05, MR-16; A8.8: MR-05, MR-08, MR-16; B1.2: MR-05, MR-16       |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 12287 and its IRR (2026); NDRRMC-OCD CP Guidebook (2020), Chapter IV |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 3-6 (contingency plans); SOP GOV-05                                 |\n\n**Table 4.21**\n\n*SOP 4-03 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Initiate</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head</td>\n<td><p>Identify the warning or scenario, source, affected area, lead time and next review.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Does the contingency plan call for heightened preparedness?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SOP 4-01 output; CP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Preparedness / PDRA initiation record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At the plan trigger</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Trigger named in the record</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Convene</td>\n<td>Research and Planning; Operations and Warning</td>\n<td><p>Notify the technical offices, barangays, utilities and partners the scenario requires.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Who must be present under the plan?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> CP; contact directory</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Notice and attendance</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> As the plan sets</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Required offices present or briefed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Compile evidence</td>\n<td>Research and Planning</td>\n<td><p>Gather hazard, exposure, vulnerability, capacity, critical facility, access, shelter, resource and service status.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is the evidence current?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> CDRA; Chapter 3 registers (Form 3-05); CP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> PDRA / impact summary, EWR-F04 (MODE GOV-F09)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before options</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source and date for each input</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Data owners</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Validate and qualify</td>\n<td>Research and Planning with sector owners</td>\n<td><p>Separate verified facts, estimates, assumptions and unknowns.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Data owners correct their own data</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> PDRA summary</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Validation and uncertainty log</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before options</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Assumptions labelled</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sector office heads</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Develop options</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head with offices</td>\n<td><p>Assess monitoring, prepositioning, warning, evacuation readiness, service protection, EOC activation and external assistance.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> A State of Imminent Disaster is assessed only through SOP GOV-05</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Validated summary</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Options and recommendation matrix</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each option names its office</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Decide and assign</td>\n<td>Authorised officials</td>\n<td><p>Route decisions; assign offices, due times and resources.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Decision by the competent authority</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Options matrix</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Decision and action register</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each action has an owner and due time</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC; RDRRMC VIII through SOP GOV-05 where relevant</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Reassess</td>\n<td>Research and Planning; Operations and Warning</td>\n<td><p>Update when the official product, observation or local situation changes materially.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Material change?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> New products; field reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> PDRA update and revision log</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> As the plan sets; no universal interval</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Earlier versions kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** At each approved warning/scenario trigger and whenever a material source or impact change occurs. Frequency is set by the relevant contingency plan; do not create a universal interval.\n\n**Escalation:** CDRRMO Head; Mayor/CDRRMC; EOC Manager when activated; technical agencies and sector office heads for specialist issues.\n\n**Minimum records:** Initiation record; source products; attendance; PDRA/impact summary; validation log; option matrix; decision/action register.\n\n## SOP 4-04 \\| EOC activation, scaling and staffing notification\n\nProcess owner: Official designated in the EOC EO authorises activation; EOC Manager implements. Purpose: Activate the EOC under approved local authority and configure a scenario-appropriate staff and liaison arrangement.\n\n**Table 4.22**\n\n*SOP 4-04 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                      |\n|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-EOC-ACTIVATE (6 steps)                                                                            |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Official designated in the EOC EO; the LGU raises its level by EO on LDRRMC recommendation (DILG VIII s. IV.3) |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | EOC Manager implements                                                                                         |\n| **Trigger**                     | An adopted activation trigger, PDRA result or incident                                                         |\n| **Forms**                       | EOC-F01 (MODE EOC-ACT-01); EOC-F02; EOC-F04                                                                    |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | B1.2 (score 3, Medium); B1.3 (score 2, High); B1.4 (score 2, Medium); B4.2 (score 1, High)                     |\n| **Functional MR links**         | B1.2: MR-05, MR-16; B1.3: MR-05; B1.4: MR-05; B4.2: MR-05                                                      |\n| **Policy basis**                | NDRRMC Memo 131 s. 2018; DILG VIII Res. No. 12-006 s. IV.3                                                     |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP HR-06 (designations); SOP 3-7 (alternate EOC)                                                              |\n\n**Table 4.23**\n\n*SOP 4-04 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Trigger check</td>\n<td>Operations and Warning; EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Compare the warning or incident information with the approved activation provisions and scenario module.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Does an adopted trigger apply? Regional triggers (Annex 4-C) are reference only</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SOP 4-01 to 4-03 outputs; EOC EO; CP</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Activation trigger assessment</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On the trigger</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Provision cited by number</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Recommend the posture</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head</td>\n<td><p>Recommend White, Blue or Red and the functions needed; obtain the CDRRMC recommendation where required.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which level and functions?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Trigger assessment</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Recommendation and proposed roster</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Recommendation separate from decision</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Authorise</td>\n<td>Official designated in the EOC EO</td>\n<td><p>Decide and record the activation and level, by Executive Order or order where required.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Only the designated official decides</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Recommendation</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Activation record, EOC-F01 (MODE EOC-ACT-01); order</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> In MODE a level change is an online authority action by an authorised role; it is never queued</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMC; OCD VIII where required</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Notify personnel</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Contact primary staff, alternates, section leads and cluster or liaison desks; log non-response and fallback.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Primary unavailable? Call the alternate</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Designation register (SOP HR-06, Annex 2-D)</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Activation notification register</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Immediately after authorisation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Every seat filled or the gap recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Configure the EOC</td>\n<td>EOC Manager; section leads</td>\n<td><p>Confirm facility safety, communications, staffing, roster, equipment, records, maps and data, and shifts.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Facility safe and working? If not, use the alternate EOC (PSCP, SOP 3-7)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Opening checklist</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> EOC opening checklist, EOC-F02</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the first briefing</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each item checked or its gap assigned</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Brief and set the rhythm</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Set initial objectives, operational period, meetings, reporting cut-offs and escalation route.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Reporting cut-offs follow DILG VIII (section 11.2)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Situation; objectives</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Initial briefing record, EOC-F04; operational plan</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At opening</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Cut-offs written in the plan</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Review the level</td>\n<td>EOC Manager; CDRRMO Head</td>\n<td><p>Review incident changes and recommend scaling up or down through the approved authority.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Change of level warranted?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SitReps; IC updates</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Level review and decision log</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each operational period</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Every level change has an authorised decision</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Designated official</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** Upon approved trigger/recommendation; immediate notification after authorisation; review according to the approved contingency plan and incident changes.\n\n**Escalation:** Mayor or official designated by EOC EO; CDRRMC; CDRRMO Head; EOC Manager; OCD Region VIII where required by local/regional arrangements.\n\n**Minimum records:** Activation decision; trigger assessment; notification register; roster; EOC opening checklist; briefing record; level review log.\n\n## SOP 4-05 \\| Initial incident coordination and EOC–ICS interface\n\nProcess owner: EOC Manager; Incident Commander/IMT retains field command. Purpose: Establish a coordinated operational picture and support the Incident Commander/IMT without duplicating field command.\n\n**Table 4.24**\n\n*SOP 4-05 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-ICS-INTERFACE (7 steps, new)                                                  |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | The Incident Commander / IMT keeps field command; Mayor/CDRRMC for policy                  |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | EOC Manager                                                                                |\n| **Trigger**                     | Notification of an incident needing EOC coordination                                       |\n| **Forms**                       | EOC-F03; EOC-F04; ER-F02                                                                   |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | A8.1 (score 2, High); B6.1 (score 1, High); B1.4 (score 2, Medium); B1.5 (score 2, Medium) |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A8.1: MR-05; B6.1: MR-08; B1.4: MR-05; B1.5: MR-05                                         |\n| **Policy basis**                | NDRRMC MC No. 4 s. 2012 (ICS); NDRRMC Memo 131 s. 2018; CP Guidebook CP Forms 10, 11       |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 6-GIS-01 (Geo-COP); SOP 4-07                                                           |\n\n**Table 4.25**\n\n*SOP 4-05 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Confirm command</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Confirm the incident, location, Incident Commander / IMT, command post and contact method.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is an Incident Commander designated?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Incident notification</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Incident and command contact record, EOC-F03</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On notification</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Positions recorded, not personal names</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor if no IC is designated</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Establish the situation</td>\n<td>EOC situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Collect time-stamped reports with source and validation status; map the affected area; list gaps.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Verified or preliminary?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Barangay, IC and agency reports; Geo-COP (SOP 6-GIS-01)</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Initial situation board</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> First hour</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Unverified items visibly marked</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Align objectives</td>\n<td>EOC Manager with the IC / IMT</td>\n<td><p>Receive incident objectives and operational period; set EOC support objectives and decisions needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> The EOC supports; it does not command the field</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> IC objectives</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> EOC support objectives (EOC-F03)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each operational period</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Objectives traceable to the IC</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC for policy decisions</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Activate functions</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Seat only the EOC sections and cluster or liaison desks the incident needs; confirm leads.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which functions does the scenario need?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Objectives; scenario module</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Section and liaison activation roster</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> As needed</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Unneeded desks not opened</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Coordinate requests</td>\n<td>EOC sections</td>\n<td><p>Route resource and service requests to their owners; track decision and fulfilment.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Owner and authority clear?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Requests from the IC, barangays and clusters</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Request tracker; deployment record, ER-F02</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Continuous</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each request has a status</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> SOP 4-07; sector office heads</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Brief decision-makers</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Prepare concise updates for the Mayor/CDRRMC and the Incident Commander.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Decisions needed now?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Situation board; requests</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Briefing note, EOC-F04; SitRep input</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> As the rhythm sets</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Source and time on every figure</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Hand over</td>\n<td>Outgoing section leads</td>\n<td><p>Transfer status, requests, decisions, risks and tasks to the next period or shift.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Anything left without an owner?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Board; logs</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Handover record, EOC-F04</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each shift change</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Incoming lead acknowledges</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** On initial incident notification; then aligned with the operational period and approved reporting rhythm.\n\n**Escalation:** Incident Commander/IMT for field command; EOC Manager for EOC coordination; Mayor/CDRRMC for policy/executive decisions; relevant office head for sector issues.\n\n**Minimum records:** Incident record; command contact; situation board; objectives; section roster; resource request tracker; briefing/SitRep inputs; handover.\n\n## SOP 4-06 \\| Evacuation coordination and monitoring\n\nProcess owner: Decision authority: official/body specified by law and City issuance; CDRRMO coordinates technical inputs; CSWDO and relevant offices lead assigned services. Purpose: Coordinate an authorised evacuation decision and monitor its implementation in a safe, accessible and accountable manner.\n\n**Table 4.26**\n\n*SOP 4-06 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                          |\n|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-EVACUATION (6 steps, new)                                                             |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | The official or body named by law and City issuance; this MOO creates no power to order evacuation |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | CDRRMO coordinates; CSWDO leads camp management                                                    |\n| **Trigger**                     | An official warning, PDRA or incident report showing people may need to move                       |\n| **Forms**                       | ER-F01; ER-F03; EWR-F03 (MODE EOC-WARN-02)                                                         |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | A6.2 (score 2, High); A7.4 (score 2, High); A7.6 (score 3, Low); A7.9 (score 1, Medium)            |\n| **Functional MR links**         | A6.2: MR-06, MR-16; A7.4: MR-04; A7.6: MR-04, MR-09, MR-16, MR-18; A7.9: MR-04, MR-18              |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121; RA 12076; RA 10821; DSWD-DILG-DOH-DepEd JMC No. 2 s. 2021 (CCCM and IDP protection)      |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 4-02; SOP 3-9 (inclusion)                                                                      |\n\n**Table 4.27**\n\n*SOP 4-06 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Assess the need</td>\n<td>CDRRMO with CSWDO and barangays</td>\n<td><p>Review warning, impact, lead time, exposure, vulnerable groups, routes and facility suitability.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is movement of people needed, and where to?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SOP 4-01 to 4-03 outputs; EC list (RA 12076)</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Evacuation assessment note</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Facility suitability checked, not assumed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Recommend; the authority decides</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head; competent authority</td>\n<td><p>Prepare options and route them; record scope, timing, sites and instruction.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Only the official or body named by law and City issuance orders evacuation</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Assessment note</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Authorised decision or order; ER-F01</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the lead time</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Authority and issuance cited</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Communicate</td>\n<td>Warning focal person; barangays</td>\n<td><p>Issue the approved message through approved channels and barangay relays, in accessible formats.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved text only</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Decision</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Message and dissemination log, EWR-F03 (MODE EOC-WARN-02)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Acknowledgement sought from each barangay</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> SOP 4-02 step 6</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Prepare services</td>\n<td>Lead offices (CSWDO, CHO, PNP, Engineering)</td>\n<td><p>Coordinate transport, traffic, receiving sites, health, protection, WASH, security and camp management.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Camp Management Committee active (JMC No. 2 s. 2021)?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Camp management plan; resource map</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Evacuation support checklist; ER-F03</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before arrival at the sites</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> DAFAC registration by the CSWDO; no names in EOC records</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sector office heads</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Monitor</td>\n<td>EOC situation unit; barangay liaison</td>\n<td><p>Receive aggregate barangay and centre status, access issues, unmet needs and safety incidents.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Blank is "not reported", never zero</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Barangay and centre reports</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Evacuation status register, ER-F01</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each reporting period</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Counts only (RA 10173)</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Review or return</td>\n<td>Competent authority</td>\n<td><p>Route continuation, change or return; record the safety check and support.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is return safe, per the competent technical office?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Status; technical clearance</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Decision and closure record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> When conditions change</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Return decided by the same authority</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** As stated in the approved evacuation protocol and hazard-specific contingency plan; update when conditions or facility status change.\n\n**Escalation:** Mayor/authorised official; CDRRMC; Incident Commander where field operations are underway; CSWDO/CHO/Engineering/PNP/BFP and barangay leads within their mandates.\n\n**Minimum records:** Assessment note; approval/order; message log; support checklist; aggregate evacuation status; closure record.\n\n## SOP 4-07 \\| Resource request coordination and mutual-aid escalation\n\nProcess owner: EOC Manager / Logistics function; approval and expenditure authority remains with competent offices under Chapter 5. Purpose: Coordinate operational resource requests from receipt to fulfilment or referral while maintaining financial and property controls.\n\n**Table 4.28**\n\n*SOP 4-07 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                         |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-RESOURCE-REQUEST (7 steps, new); MODE EOC → Requests |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Approval and expenditure by the competent offices under Chapter 5 |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | EOC Manager / Logistics                                           |\n| **Trigger**                     | A resource or service request during an activation                |\n| **Forms**                       | EOC-F06                                                           |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | B6.2 (score 1, High); A8.3 (score 3, Low); A7.5 (score 4, Low)    |\n| **Functional MR links**         | B6.2: MR-08; A8.3: MR-05, MR-08; A7.5: MR-04, MR-08               |\n| **Policy basis**                | RA 10121 Sec. 21; RA 12009 and its IRR                            |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 5; SOP 4-05                                               |\n\n**Table 4.29**\n\n*SOP 4-07 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Receive and log</td>\n<td>EOC Logistics</td>\n<td><p>Record requester, incident, item or service, quantity, location, purpose, priority and time needed.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Complete enough to act?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Request</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Resource request record, EOC-F06; MODE EOC → Requests</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On receipt</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Every request logged, including verbal ones</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Check completeness</td>\n<td>EOC Logistics</td>\n<td><p>Clarify purpose, specification, delivery point and requesting authority.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Is the requester authorised?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Request record</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Completeness check</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before availability check</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Gaps returned to the requester</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Check availability</td>\n<td>Logistics with the asset owner</td>\n<td><p>Check stock, condition, location, committed quantity and mobilisation.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Available locally?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Inventories</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Availability and status record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Urgency-specific</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Asset owner confirms</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Asset owner office head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Route approval</td>\n<td>Authorised office (Chapter 5)</td>\n<td><p>Refer expenditure, procurement, transfer or release to the authorised official.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approval follows Chapter 5; this chapter creates no spending power</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Availability record</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Approval or refusal and basis</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Urgency-specific</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Basis recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> City Mayor; Budget, Accounting, Procurement, Property</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Mobilise and track</td>\n<td>EOC Logistics</td>\n<td><p>Record dispatch, carrier, expected arrival, receipt, partial fulfilment and custody.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Delivered as requested?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Approval</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Movement and delivery record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Until receipt</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Custody recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Escalate the gap</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Request mutual aid or higher-level support through the approved route.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Local resources insufficient?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Availability record</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> External assistance request and response</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Urgency-specific</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Route as agreed with the Province and OCD VIII</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Provincial, regional and NGA channels</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Close and reconcile</td>\n<td>EOC Logistics with the asset owner</td>\n<td><p>Record use, return, demobilisation, outstanding balance, damage and replenishment.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Anything outstanding?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Delivery records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Closeout and reconciliation (EOC-F06)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At closure</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Balances agree with records</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Chapter 5 offices</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** Urgency-specific; maintain status until complete or formally referred/closed.\n\n**Escalation:** EOC Manager; CDRRMO Head; Budget/Accounting/Procurement/Property officials and City Mayor as required; provincial/regional/NGA coordination channels.\n\n**Minimum records:** Request record; completeness/availability check; authority decision; dispatch/delivery evidence; external assistance record; closeout.\n\n## SOP 4-08 \\| SitRep, operational briefing and reporting submission\n\nProcess owner: EOC Planning / situation unit; authorised reviewing/approving official per reporting instructions. Purpose: Produce timely and traceable operational reports using the current authorised reporting template.\n\n**Table 4.30**\n\n*SOP 4-08 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-SITREP-CYCLE (5 steps); MODE EOC → SitReps                                  |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | The approving official in the reporting route                                            |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | EOC Planning / situation unit                                                            |\n| **Trigger**                     | Each reporting period under the alert status in force                                    |\n| **Forms**                       | EOC-F05 (MODE EOC-SITREP-01)                                                             |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | B5.1 (score 2, High); B5.2 (score 1, High); B1.5 (score 2, Medium); A10.3 (score 4, Low) |\n| **Functional MR links**         | B5.1: MR-07; B5.2: MR-07; B1.5: MR-05; A10.3: MR-02, MR-07                               |\n| **Policy basis**                | DILG VIII Memorandum R08-LGCDD-2025-02-26-008, Tables 3 and 4                            |\n| **Cross-references**            | SOP 4-05, 4-06                                                                           |\n\n**Table 4.31**\n\n*SOP 4-08 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Set the cut-off</td>\n<td>EOC Planning / situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Confirm reporting period, data cut-off, deadline and the current template.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Which DILG VIII deadline applies to this alert status?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Alert status; DILG VIII Table 3</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Reporting schedule</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Each period</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Template version noted</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Request updates</td>\n<td>Situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Ask barangays, clusters, the IC / IMT, utilities and sector offices for updates.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All expected sources asked?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Contact list</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Input request and receipt log</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the cut-off</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Missing reports listed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Barangay liaison</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Validate</td>\n<td>Situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Check dates, geography, totals, duplicates, units, missing fields and source status.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Blank stays blank: never converted to zero</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Inputs</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Validation checklist</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before drafting</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Discrepancies sent back to the source</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Source or sector office</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Draft the report</td>\n<td>Situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Summarise situation, impact, actions, resources, needs, gaps, decisions, maps and next steps.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Pre-, during-, post- or terminal report?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Validated data</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> SitRep draft</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before review</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Harmonized template used</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Review and approve</td>\n<td>EOC Manager; approving official</td>\n<td><p>Obtain technical and management review and approval.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Approved for release?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Draft</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Approved report and review history</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before the deadline</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Approved SitReps are locked in MODE</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Submit and archive</td>\n<td>Situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Send to the designated recipient; keep the copy, attachments, time sent and receipt.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Deadline met?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Approved report</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Submission and archive register, EOC-F05 (MODE EOC-SITREP-01)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> On or before the cut-off</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Time sent recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> DILG VIII / Province / OCD VIII</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Correct or update</td>\n<td>Situation unit</td>\n<td><p>Issue a corrected or superseding report openly; keep the prior version and reason.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Material error found?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Feedback</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Correction and version record</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> As soon as found</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Prior version kept</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** Use current DILG Region VIII/OCD/NDRRMC reporting cut-offs; update for each operational reporting period or required pre/post/terminal report.\n\n**Escalation:** EOC Manager; CDRRMO Head; DILG VIII/OCD VIII as reporting recipients; source/sector offices for material data discrepancies.\n\n**Minimum records:** Schedule; input logs; validation; approved SitRep; supporting source annexes; submission receipt; correction record.\n\n## SOP 4-09 \\| EOC deactivation, transition and after-action review\n\nProcess owner: Deactivation authority: official designated in EOC EO; EOC Manager coordinates handover and closeout. Purpose: Close the activated EOC in a controlled manner and transfer unresolved responsibilities to permanent and recovery/continuity arrangements.\n\n**Table 4.32**\n\n*SOP 4-09 Control Block*\n\n| **Control element**             | **Entry**                                                                                                         |\n|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Type and MODE template**      | Protocol: PR-EOC-DEACTIVATE (7 steps, new)                                                                        |\n| **Decision authority (legal)**  | Official designated in the EOC EO, on the IC recommendation                                                       |\n| **Process owner (operational)** | EOC Manager coordinates handover and closeout                                                                     |\n| **Trigger**                     | Incident stabilised; IC recommends termination                                                                    |\n| **Forms**                       | EOC-F01 (MODE EOC-ACT-01); ER-F05; ER-F06                                                                         |\n| **IAT v1.6 indicators**         | B1.3 (score 2, High); B7.4 (score 2, Medium); A10.6 (score 4, Low)                                                |\n| **Functional MR links**         | B1.3: MR-05; B7.4: MR-04, MR-11; A10.6: MR-07, MR-11                                                              |\n| **Policy basis**                | NDRRMC Memo 131 s. 2018; CP Guidebook (2020) Chapter IV; NEDA Disaster Rehabilitation and Recovery Planning Guide |\n| **Cross-references**            | Chapter 7 (learning); Chapter 8 (recovery)                                                                        |\n\n**Table 4.33**\n\n*SOP 4-09 Steps and Controls*\n\n<table style="width:100%;">\n<colgroup>\n<col style="width: 11%" />\n<col style="width: 15%" />\n<col style="width: 30%" />\n<col style="width: 22%" />\n<col style="width: 21%" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr class="header">\n<th><strong>Step</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Actor</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Action and decision rule</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Inputs and outputs / records</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Timing, control and escalation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>1. Review stabilisation</td>\n<td>EOC Manager with the IC</td>\n<td><p>Assess threat, activities, outstanding needs, service status, resource commitments and reporting duties.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> The IC recommends termination (CP Guidebook, 2020)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> SitReps; IC update</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Deactivation readiness checklist</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> After stabilisation</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Outstanding items listed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>2. Recommend and approve</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head; designated official</td>\n<td><p>Prepare the recommendation and obtain the deactivation decision.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Only the designated official deactivates</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Readiness checklist</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Deactivation decision, EOC-F01 (MODE EOC-ACT-01)</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At once</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Online authority action in MODE</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Mayor/CDRRMC</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>3. Notify</td>\n<td>EOC Manager</td>\n<td><p>Inform EOC staff, clusters, barangays, partners and reporting recipients.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> All recipients reached?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Decision</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Deactivation notice and acknowledgements</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Immediately</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Acknowledgements recorded</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>4. Transfer</td>\n<td>EOC Manager; receiving offices</td>\n<td><p>Assign outstanding tasks, requests, monitoring, information, continuity and recovery tasks to named offices.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Does each item have a receiving office?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Open items</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Transition and handover register, ER-F05</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Before closing</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Receiving office acknowledges</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Sector office heads; Chapter 8 owner</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>5. Close the records</td>\n<td>Records custodian</td>\n<td><p>Complete the logbook index, SitReps, decisions, resource records, maps and evidence archive.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Complete?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> All records</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Record closeout register</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> At closing</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Terminal report filed</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> EOC Manager</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="even">\n<td>6. Review performance</td>\n<td>CDRRMO with the offices</td>\n<td><p>Hold a hotwash or AAR; identify system causes; agree corrective actions.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> System causes, not blame</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> Records; participant input</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> AAR and corrective action record, ER-F06</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> Within the period set by the MOO quality procedure</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Each action has an owner and due date</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> Chapter 7 owner; CDRRMC oversight</p></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class="odd">\n<td>7. Update the controls</td>\n<td>CDRRMO Head</td>\n<td><p>Revise training, plans, contacts and procedures through document control.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision:</strong> Change needed in a controlled document?</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>In:</strong> AAR</p>\n<p><strong>Out:</strong> Revision request and controlled update</p></td>\n<td><p><strong>Time:</strong> After the AAR</p>\n<p><strong>Control:</strong> Changes approved before use</p>\n<p><strong>Escalate:</strong> CDRRMO Head</p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n**Timing / frequency:** After incident stabilisation as determined by competent authority; after-action review within the period set by the approved MOO quality procedure.\n\n**Escalation:** Mayor/CDRRMC; CDRRMO Head; EOC Manager; Incident Commander/IMT; sector office heads; Chapter 7 M&E process owner.\n\n**Minimum records:** Readiness checklist; decision; notification; transition register; records index; AAR; corrective action and revision records.\n\n# 15. Responsibility Assignment (RACI)\n\nThe following RACI is a proposed operational assignment for validation. It clarifies who performs work; it does not transfer statutory powers, professional accountability, command authority or financial/procurement responsibility. “A” is the single proposed process-accountable owner for the operational task; “R” performs the work; “C” is consulted; “I” is informed. Where a legal decision belongs to a named official/body, that authority is stated separately.\n\n**Table 4.34**\n\n*Proposed EOC and Incident Coordination RACI*\n\n| **Activity**                                      | **Mayor / CDRRMC**                  | **CDRRMO Head**             | **Ops & Warning** | **EOC Manager / sections** | **IC / IMT**        | **Sector offices / utilities** | **Barangays**          |\n|---------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-----------------------------|-------------------|----------------------------|---------------------|--------------------------------|------------------------|\n| Routine monitoring and warning receipt            | I                                   | A                           | R                 | I                          | I                   | C                              | C                      |\n| Technical warning interpretation                  | I                                   | A                           | R/C               | C                          | C                   | R/C source owners              | C                      |\n| Warning-action recommendation                     | A where executive decision required | A/R technical process       | R                 | C                          | C                   | C                              | C                      |\n| Approval of evacuation / public protective action | A per law/issuance                  | R/C recommendation          | C                 | C                          | C                   | C                              | R implementation       |\n| EOC activation authorisation                      | A / designated authority            | R recommendation            | C                 | R implementation           | I                   | I                              | I                      |\n| EOC coordination and reporting                    | I / policy decisions                | A (institutional oversight) | R support         | R                          | C                   | R/C                            | R/C                    |\n| Field incident command                            | I as appropriate                    | I / support                 | C                 | C/support                  | A/R                 | R within agency command        | R within local mandate |\n| Sector response services                          | I                                   | C                           | C                 | C/coordination             | A/R where appointed | A/R by statutory sector lead   | R local support        |\n| Resource request coordination                     | I / approval as required            | A                           | C                 | R                          | R requests          | R asset owner                  | R requests/status      |\n| SitRep preparation and submission                 | I / review                          | A oversight                 | C                 | R                          | R inputs            | R inputs                       | R inputs               |\n| Deactivation / transition                         | A / designated authority            | R recommendation            | C                 | R coordination             | C                   | R sector handover              | R local handover       |\n| AAR and corrective action                         | I / oversight                       | A                           | R                 | R                          | C                   | R for own actions              | R for own actions      |\n\n| VALIDATION NOTE. The RACI must be reconciled with the actual EOC EO, ICS EO, cluster membership, approved organisational appointments and current contingency plans. For evacuation and other statutory decisions, the legally competent authority is the “A” regardless of the operational RACI notation. |\n|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n\nAnnex 4-B repeats the RACI with a separate column for the legal decision authority, so that operational accountability (A) is never read as a legal power.\n\n# 16. Performance Monitoring, Quality Assurance and Corrective Action\n\nPerformance shall be monitored through a small set of operationally meaningful measures and evidence. Targets and reporting frequencies are established by approved City issuances, contingency plans and the EOC EO. This draft does not impose unsupported numerical service-level targets.\n\n**Table 4.35**\n\n*Performance Areas, Measures and Review Owners*\n\n| **Performance area**              | **Suggested measure / evidence**                                                                                                     | **Review owner**                                   |\n|-----------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|\n| Warning provenance and timeliness | Warning records with complete source, issue/receipt time, validity and supersession fields; elapsed time from receipt to escalation. | Operations and Warning; CDRRMO Head                |\n| Dissemination and acknowledgement | Messages with recorded approval, channel, target area and acknowledgement/failure follow-up.                                         | Designated warning/public information focal person |\n| Activation readiness              | Activations with valid authority, completed notification, assigned roles, opening checklist and briefing evidence.                   | EOC Manager / CDRRMO Head                          |\n| EOC–ICS coordination              | Incidents with named Incident Commander/IMT, clear command liaison, objectives, resource request traceability and handover.          | EOC Manager / Incident Commander                   |\n| Barangay reporting                | Barangay status reports with time, source, validation and data completeness; missing reports explicitly identified.                  | Barangay liaison / EOC situation unit              |\n| SitRep/reporting quality          | Reports submitted using current template, with source and verification status, review and submission receipts.                       | EOC Planning / CDRRMO Head                         |\n| Protective action and evacuation  | Approved decisions, dissemination, implementation monitoring, safe receiving arrangements and return/closure evidence.               | Lead authority/sector office; CDRRMO coordination  |\n| Exercises and learning            | Plans tested; findings assigned; corrective actions verified and reflected in revised plans/protocols.                               | CDRRMO Head / CDRRMC oversight                     |\n\nCorrective actions shall identify the finding, evidence, cause or contributing condition, action required, accountable owner, supporting offices, due date, resource implication, verification evidence and closure decision. Repeated or high-consequence non-closure shall be escalated through the CDRRMO Head, the appropriate executive/sector office and the CDRRMC oversight mechanism.\n\n# 17. Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities\n\nThe following items are derived from the assessment references and operational gaps explicitly described in Chapters 1–3 and from the repository architecture. Annex 4-A gives the exact owner, target and status of each A6, A7, A8 and B1.2–B1.5 row from the IAT v1.6 Action Plan; the references below use its priorities.\n\n**Table 4.36**\n\n*Implementation, Validation and Institutionalisation Priorities*\n\n| **Priority / reference**                                                             | **Required action**                                                                                                                                                                                             | **Proposed accountable lead**                                                                | **Supporting actors**                                                | **Evidence of completion / validation**                                                                          |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| P1 – B1.1 (Ch.1 assessment narrative)                                                | Issue the local EOC-establishing EO defining authority, relationship with the OpCen/CDRRMO, activation levels, EOC Manager, coordination interfaces and ICS boundary.                                           | Mayor / City Legal Office route; CDRRMO Head process lead                                    | CDRRMC; OCD VIII; response clusters                                  | Signed EO, legal review, approved structure and implementation notice.                                           |\n| P1 – B6.1 (Ch.1 assessment narrative)                                                | Approve the ICS–EOC interface and chain of command: EOC supports the Incident Commander and does not command field operations.                                                                                  | Mayor / CDRRMO Head within approval route                                                    | City Legal Office; OCD VIII; IMT/response clusters                   | Approved ICS/EOC issuance, RACI, command/coordination diagram and exercise evidence.                             |\n| P1 – B1.3 (High); B1.2, B1.4, B1.5 (Medium) (IAT v1.6)                               | Confirm EOC concept of operations, activation/deactivation authority and scenarios, and incorporate the validated operating levels and scenario modules in the EO and contingency plans.                        | CDRRMO Head / designated EOC Manager                                                         | CDRRMC; partner offices; OCD VIII; City Legal Office                 | Approved EOC CONOPS and scenario matrix, controlled trigger records and tabletop/functional exercise.            |\n| P1 – A6.2, A6.3, A6.7 (High); A6.1 (Medium) (IAT v1.6)                               | Complete the warning-to-action matrix for priority hazards with official trigger sources, legal decision authorities, message approval, multi-channel dissemination and acknowledgement evidence.               | CDRRMO Operations and Warning                                                                | PAGASA; PHIVOLCS; MGB; barangays; public information; sector offices | Validated warning matrix, SOP 4-01/4-02, source register, message templates and exercise/AAR.                    |\n| P1 – A7.4, A8.1, A8.2, A8.8, A8.9 (High); A7.9, A8.4, A8.6, A8.7 (Medium) (IAT v1.6) | Document and test evacuation, response-service coordination, shelter/CCCM, inclusion, reporting and field-to-EOC interfaces in hazard-specific plans.                                                           | CDRRMO Head as coordinator; statutory lead offices for each service                          | CSWDO; CHO; PNP; BFP; barangays; Engineering; DepEd; partners        | Approved protocols, lead/support assignments, site/service status, exercise and after-action evidence.           |\n'
